We could certainly stop using automagic IO and retrieve all files references as current metadata objects in one go. However, using automagic IO at least points out the issues that it has. This is the one and only place where we do this.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520259502,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDQzMjcxMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2261#issuecomment-370432713"},"message":"OK, whoever wrote AutomagicIO... #2255 has abandoned it -- caused to many complaints...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520261003,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDQ0MDUzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2261#issuecomment-370440539"},"message":"Current state of #2255 now gives one single progressbar for obtaining all needed metadata blobs. Makes it not a single second faster, but less \"flood\"-like with an idea on how many files and how heavy they are:\n```\n[INFO   ] Actually getting 489 files \nTotal (115 ok out of 489) 38%|██████████████████████                                    | 3.22M/8.47M [02:49\u003c51:29, 1.70KB/s]\n```\n\nSidenote: the \"actually getting\" is an old-timer, i know, but it still sounds as if datalad is surprised by itself. In this context, and quite a few others it makes no sense to log this, with this wording, and at this level.\n\nIn my test case above just shy of 500 files have to be obtained via SSH, and it seems that they are obtained one by one, strictly serial,. Not sure if there is a dedicated authentication run for each of them. There is about one second delay between two files.\n\nIf you want to try:\n\n```\n% datalad install -s smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets-meta6-4/datalad/crawl hotnewshit\n% datalad search haxby\ndatalad search haxby  36.74s user 12.24s system 8% cpu 9:46.15 total\n```\n\n(nine minutes waiting for IO)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520261091,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDQ0MTA3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2261#issuecomment-370441076"},"message":"Closing, as the core issue has been dealt with. We still have have #2262 as a general OMG-this-is-bad outburst ;-)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520261261,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUwNDI2Nzk3Nw=="},"status":2}]}